2. **Optimizing job recommendation**
        a. What I have realized is that the only one job description is sent to the LLM for recommendation.
        This is not optimal because the LLM will only recommend projects based on one job description.
        And if I send multiple job descriptions, the LLM will be able to recommend projects that are relevant to multiple job descriptions.
           => This may bring a token max problem because we will be sending bunch of text.
           => But if we don't care about the max token limit, we face a problem of reengineering our prompts and schema
           to match the current demand from the LLM.
                => The current demand will include:
                    1. Telling the LLM to recommend relevant projects for each of the job descriptions and titles sent.
                    2. Reengineer code to send two job titles with their descriptions to the LLM.
                    3. Extract two job titles and descriptions from the database.
           POSSIBLE SOLUTIONS:
                1. Send multiple job descriptions and titles to the LLM in one prompt, and ask it to recommend relevant projects for each of them.
                2. Send multiple job descriptions and titles to the LLM in one prompt, and ask it to recommend relevant projects for all of them combined.
                3. Send multiple job descriptions and titles to the LLM in one prompt, and ask it to recommend relevant projects for each of them, but limit the number of recommendations per job description/title.
                4. Use multiple openrouter api calls. Thus each call handles a job description and title, and then combine the results.


